    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci` through the CLI, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by Commander.js's main program option parsing and not passed through to the frai-gate subcommand.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI modified the `gate` command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754) to extract all arguments from `process.argv` that come after the `gate` command. This ensures flags like `--ci` are preserved and passed through to the frai-gate CLI, regardless of how Commander.js parses them.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Updated the `gate` command handler to use `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)` to get all remaining arguments\n- This approach is more reliable than relying on Commander.js's variadic argument parsing\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 `frai gate init` still works correctly without `--ci`, creating only `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- \u2705 No changes were made to `packages/frai-gate` as requested",
